The build log shows a clear failure in the %check section: '/usr/bin/python3.13: No module named pytest'. The spec file attempts to run `%python_exec -m pytest tests`, but `pytest` is not available in the build environment. This is a classic missing `BuildRequires` issue. The package uses `pyproject.toml` (indicated by `%pyproject_wheel` and `%pyproject_install`), so the correct fix is to add `BuildRequires: %{python_module pytest}`. Other issues in the original spec include: 1) `%pyton_wheel` typo (should be `%pyproject_wheel`), 2) `%setup` vs `%autosetup`, 3) `%fdupes` using `%{python_sitelib}` instead of `%{python3_sitelib}`, 4) `%files` using `%{python_sitelib}` and a `.dist-info` path that doesn't match pyproject standards (should be egg-info or just the package dir). The user wants only the raw spec file content.